\par\par \b \uc2 Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Euro's Rise Tempered Ahead Of Florida G7  \b0\par\par\uc2 401 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Januar 2004\par 07:44\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monetary authorities, which have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily to stem the yen's rapid rise against the dollar, seemed happy about Trichet's remarks and sought to portray the ECB as joining Tokyo in openly fretting about the dollar's fall.  \par \par \uc2 Zembei Mizoguchi, Japan's vice finance minister for international affairs, told reporters Tuesday that Europe, like Japan, "seems to think that rapid moves in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates are inappropriate."  \par \par \uc2 But Masamichi Koike, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  spot trading at Sumitomo Mitsui Banking Corp., warned that U.S. nonchalance over the dollar's weakness, as shown in the lack of any reference to the issue in the G10 communique, will prevent the dollar from staging any significant rebound against other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  for now.  \par \par \uc2 "As long as the U.S. remains unconcerned about the dollar's current weakness, there's not much Europe and Japan can do" to change the dollar-bearish trend, Koike said.  \par \par \uc2 With the U.S. likely to maintain its benign neglect of the dollar's slide, few traders expect finance ministers and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chiefs of the Group of Seven industrial powers to offer any unified support for the beleaguered U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  when they meet Feb. 6-7 in Florida.  \par \par \uc2 Still, many market players expect the euro to remain in an adjustment phase against the dollar until the G7 meeting, as traders are wary of chasing it higher in case there are any surprises from the meeting.  \par \par \uc2 Commerzbank's Muramatsu predicts that it will take some time for the euro to test new highs past $1.2900 since its recent rise has been "too fast."  \par \par \uc2 But he is bullish about the euro's prospects post-G7, warning that nothing will prevent the euro from charging past $1.3000 and testing $1.3500 if the G7 nations "fail to send a clear warning against the dollar's weakness" at their upcoming meeting.  \par \par \uc2 -By Leika Kihara, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; leika.kihara@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Alastair Gale  \par \par \uc2 The chart of late Tokyo \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates that accompanied Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been replaced with an enhanced \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixture that is updated hourly.  \par \par \uc2 Subscribers can find this table:  \par \par \uc2 -On Telerate pages 4046 and 1087.  \par \par \uc2 -On Dow Jones Newswires by searching the code N/IFX  \par \par \uc2 -On Reuters by entering FRX or INT  \par \par \uc2 -On Bloomberg by entering NI FRX  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040113e01d0006q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
