\par\par \b \uc2 Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Euro Up Vs Dollar As Trichet Impact Fades  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Leika Kihara  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 843 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Januar 2004\par 06:31\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The euro rose against the dollar in Asia Tuesday, quickly recovering from initial weakness following European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Jean-Claude Trichet's expression of concern Monday about the European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent fast-paced ascent.  \par \par \uc2 The euro initially lost some ground, as players remained wary of chasing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  higher after Trichet's warning that recent moves in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets have been "brutal" and bear the hallmarks of "excessive volatility."  \par \par \uc2 But the early waves of profit taking soon gave way to non-Japanese players' active buying on dips, pushing the euro to as high as $1.2772. The euro also staged a v-shaped rebound against the yen, rising as high as Y136.03 after a drop to Y135.47.  \par \par \uc2 "We are concerned and we are certainly not indifferent" about the euro's rise, Trichet said after a meeting of central bankers from the Group of 10 leading industrial nations in Basel, Switzerland.  \par \par \uc2 Few market players in Tokyo viewed Trichet's remarks as strong enough to change the current dollar-bearish tide. Rather, the comments were seen as just a good opportunity to unload some euro long-positions for short-term gains, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 "The remarks gave the market what it needed most now - a natural, healthy correction" from the euro's staggering 5% rise against the dollar so far this year, said Ryohei Muramatsu, manager of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trade at Commerzbank's Tokyo branch.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar remained weak against the yen. After coming off an early high of Y106.72, the greenback drifted lower to hover below Y106.50, weighed on by Japanese exporters' heavy sell orders lined up around that level.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar's inability to sustain gains for even a short period of time shows how wary market players have become in buying dollars amid persistent concern over the U.S. trade and budget deficits and receding hopes of an early U.S. interest rate hike.  \par \par \uc2 At 0515 GMT, the euro was at $1.2764, higher than $1.2740 late Monday in New York. The euro was at $1.2846 in Asia Monday. Financial markets in Tokyo were closed for a holiday Monday.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar was quoted at Y106.54, below Y106.70 late Monday in New York. The dollar was at Y106.42 late Monday in Asia.  \par \par \uc2 Against the yen, the euro was quoted at Y135.98, up from Y135.95 in New York late Monday. The euro was at Y136.70 in Asia late Monday.  \par \par \uc2 Sterling was at $1.8489, up from $1.8465 in New York and higher than $1.8471 in Asia Monday.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monetary authorities, which have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily to stem the yen's rapid rise against the dollar, seemed happy about Trichet's remarks and sought to portray the ECB as joining Tokyo in openly fretting about the dollar's fall.  \par \par \uc2 Zembei Mizoguchi, Japan's vice finance minister for international affairs, told reporters Tuesday that Europe, like Japan, "seems to think that rapid moves in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates are inappropriate."  \par \par \uc2 But Masamichi Koike, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  spot trading at Sumitomo Mitsui Banking Corp., warned that U.S. nonchalance over the dollar's weakness, as shown in the lack of any reference to the issue in the G10 communique, will prevent the dollar from staging any significant rebound against other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  for now.  \par \par \uc2 "As long as the U.S. remains unconcerned about the dollar's current weakness, there's not much Europe and Japan can do" to change the dollar-bearish trend, Koike said.  \par \par \uc2 With the U.S. likely to maintain its benign neglect of the dollar's slide, few traders expect finance ministers and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chiefs of the Group of Seven industrial powers to offer any unified support for the beleaguered U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  when they meet Feb. 6-7 in Florida.  \par \par \uc2 Still, many market players expect the euro to remain in an adjustment phase against the dollar until the G7 meeting, as traders are wary of chasing it higher in case there are any surprises from the meeting.  \par \par \uc2 Commerzbank's Muramatsu predicts that it will take some time for the euro to test new highs past $1.2900 since its recent rise has been "too fast."  \par \par \uc2 But he is bullish about the euro's prospects post-G7, warning that nothing will prevent the euro from charging past $1.3000 and testing $1.3500 if the G7 nations "fail to send a clear warning against the dollar's weakness" at their upcoming meeting.  \par \par \uc2 -By Leika Kihara, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; leika.kihara@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Alastair Gale  \par \par \uc2 The chart of late Tokyo \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates that accompanied Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been replaced with an enhanced \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixture that is updated hourly.  \par \par \uc2 Subscribers can find this table:  \par \par \uc2 -On Telerate pages 4046 and 1087.  \par \par \uc2 -On Dow Jones Newswires by searching the code N/IFX  \par \par \uc2 -On Reuters by entering FRX or INT  