\par\par \b \uc2 Tanigaki:  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  Mkt Shows Dlr Weakness Not Yen Strength  \b0\par\par\uc2 316 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Januar 2004\par 03:10\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The dollar's recent weakening has been too rapid considering that U.S. economic fundamentals are firm, Japan's Finance Minister said Tuesday, suggesting Tokyo believes further weakness in the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is unwarranted.  \par \par \uc2 "Currently, I believe it's more accurate to say that the dollar is weakening, rather than the yen is strengthening," Sadakazu Tanigaki told reporters when asked to comment on recent \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market conditions.  \par \par \uc2 "Considering the power of the U.S. economy, I believe that recent movements have been rather rapid," he said.  \par \par \uc2 Tanigaki noted that the dollar is also weakening against the euro, which has prompted European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Jean-Claude Trichet to express concern.  \par \par \uc2 Trichet said Monday after a meeting of central bankers from the Group of 10 leading industrial nations in Basel, Switzerland, that recent moves in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets have been "brutal" and bear the hallmarks of "excessive volatility."  \par \par \uc2 "We are concerned and we are certainly not indifferent," Trichet said.  \par \par \uc2 Japan, for its part, will continue to "take appropriate action" in the event of speculative or rapid \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market movements, Tanigaki said, underscoring the government's will to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb the yen's rise against the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 But Tanigaki refused to comment on Friday's sharp jump in the dollar, which traders attributed to large-scale yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , acting on behalf of the Finance Ministry.  \par \par \uc2 "I make it a rule not to comment on specific (exchange-rate) levels," he said.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar surged close to Y2 on Friday to a high of Y108.29 on apparent Finance Ministry-directed action, although it later retreated back to the Y106-level.  \par \par \uc2 As of 0301 GMT, the greenback was trading at Y106.56.  \par \par \uc2 -By Miyako Takebe, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; miyako.takebe@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Alastair Gale  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040113e01d00022\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
