\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-BoJ's Fukui- \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  a risk factor for everyone.   \b0\par\par\uc2 250 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Januar 2004\par 10:36\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 BASEL, Switzerland, Jan 12 (Reuters) - Bank of Japan Governor Toshihiko Fukui said on Monday that policymakers across the globe viewed \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  tensions as a risk, and that he agreed with that view.   \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  issue is an unstable factor for each country. \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  is seen as a risk factor by policymakers in relation to global imbalance issues," Fukui told reporters on the sidelines of a bi-monthly meeting of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governors at the Bank for the International Settlements.   \par \par \uc2 "The BOJ has the same view, of course," he added.   \par \par \uc2 In 2003 \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent a record 20 trillion yen in yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb an export-damaging rise in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 Fukui also said that Japan's financial system was gradually improving but that some problems remained.   \par \par \uc2 Asked whether Japan's economy was coming out of deflation, Fukui replied: "There are signs (it is). Gradually."   \par \par \uc2 "We have a firm commitment (to maintain the current accommodative policy) until we see above zero consumer inflation in a stable manner," he said.   \par \par \uc2 Under its ultra-easy monetary policy, introduced in March 2001, the BOJ floods the money market to keep interest rates near zero. It buys 1.2 trillion yen of long-term Japanese government bonds per month to boost credit market liquidity.   \par \par \uc2 Government figures released on Friday suggested Japan's economic recovery lost momentum in November as inventories of some products rose and unusual weather patterns disrupted consumer spending.    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040112e01c002k5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
