\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar hits new low against euro.  \b0\par\par\uc2 727 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Januar 2004\par 08:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Ovais Subhani\par     SINGAPORE, Jan 12 (Reuters) - The U.S. dollar hit a new low\par against the euro on Monday but found some support against the\par yen, because of fears of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par  \par     After a largely subdued session, the euro reached new highs\par above $1.2868 as European markets opened.\par     Trade had been thinned in Asia by a holiday in Japan, the\par region's largest \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market, added to the general\par reluctance to build fresh positions, dealers in Singapore said.\par     They said the market was trading cautiously ahead of a\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 briefing by European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  chief Jean-Claude Trichet at  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1200 GMT. Trichet is due to discuss Monday's meeting in Basel  \par \par \uc2 of rich-country central bankers.  \par \par \uc2 The market would sift through the briefing for any clues on  \par \par \uc2 the issue of the U.S. dollar weakness and euro's strength.  \par \par \uc2 After that, the next major opportunity to hear official views  \par \par \uc2 on exchange rates will be at the Group of Seven meeting in  \par \par \uc2 early February.  \par \par \uc2 The last G7 meeting, in September, sparked a dollar  \par \par \uc2 sell-off that has not ended yet. Since early September the euro  \par \par \uc2 has risen by about 20 percent against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,  \par \par \uc2 pulling the trade-weighted dollar to early 1996 levels.  \par \par \uc2 "The market is still short of dollars and long on euro and  \par \par \uc2 other majors so people would want to hear ECB before taking  \par \par \uc2 fresh positions," said a Singapore dealer.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     At 0730 GMT the dollar was around $1.2847 to the euro and\par 106.43 yen.\par     The dollar had hit an earlier record low of $1.2868 versus\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the euro on Friday after data showed the U.S. economy had added  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 just 1,000 jobs in December. The market had been expecting a  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 130,000 rise.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     But the U.S. unemployment rate fell to 5.7 percent, from\par 5.9 percent in November.\par     Against the yen, the dollar traded just above 106 on\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Friday, before the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and pushed it above  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 108 yen. The dollar fell back to end New York trade at 106.57  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 yen. The euro finished Friday U.S. trade at $1.2832.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar has been hobbled in recent months by low U.S.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 interest rates and a widening gap between U.S. savings and  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 investment. So far the burden of the dollar weakness has fallen  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 mainly on the euro and some other European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     Analysts said Friday's employment data backed views in the\par market that U.S. rates would continue to stay low.\par     "The employment report was a shocker and will continue to\par resonate through the week," said David Simmonds, strategist at\par Royal Bank of Scotland in Singapore.\par     "It has put back very significantly the timing the Fed\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 would be prepared to put on a rate hike and that is in turn a  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 drag on the dollar even from these heavily sold levels," he  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Philip Wee, strategist at Singapore's DBS Bank, said the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 market would also consider some other crucial data releases due  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 this week from the United States.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 He said the U.S. Fed Beige Book on Wednesday, December  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 inflation data on Thursday, and industrial production and  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 capacity utilisation on Friday would be important.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Alan Greenspan, chairman of the U.S. Federal Reserve, is  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 scheduled to speak on Tuesday in Germany. But, despite the weak  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 employment data, few expect him to depart from his recent  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 statements on monetary policy and the U.S. growth outlook.  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bid prices at 0651 GMT.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 All data taken from Reuters with percent change calculated  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 from the daily U.S. close at 2130GMT.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                      Last     US Close  %Chg   YTD %  2003 Cls\par                               .\par -------------------------------------------------------------\par Euro/dlr             1.2840   1.2832   +0.06   +2.08   1.2578\par Dlr/yen              106.43   106.57   -0.13   -0.82   107.31\par Euro/yen             136.66   136.56   +0.07   +1.21   135.03\par Dlr/swiss            1.2199   1.2206   -0.06   -1.64   1.2403\par Stg/dlr              1.8463   1.8488   -0.14   +3.43   1.7850\par Dlr/can              1.2706   1.2703   +0.02   -2.00   1.2965\par Aus/dlr              0.7777   0.7762   +0.19   +3.47   0.7516\par Euro/swiss           1.5665   1.5664   +0.01   +0.42   1.5599\par Euro/stg             0.6951   0.6938   +0.19   -1.33   0.7045.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040112e01c0028w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\