\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Silver at near-6-yr high in Asia, gold quiet.  \b0\par\par\uc2 525 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Januar 2004\par 05:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     SINGAPORE, Jan 12 (Reuters) - Silver surged in Asia on\par Monday to its highest levels in nearly six years, repeating the\par metal's strong performance in New York, while gold was flat due\par to the absence of key player Japan and a steadier dollar.\par     Spot silver        was quoted at $6.55/6.58 by 0406 GMT\par after trading as high as $6.60 an ounce, the metal's highest\par level since April 1998. Silver was last quoted in New York at\par $6.45/6.47.\par     "Silver has a better performance than gold. We feel there\par are short positions in the silver market. People need to cover\par back their positions," said one Hong Kong dealer.\par     Dealers said silver received an additional boost from\par strong base metals such as copper and nickel. It moves together\par with industrial commodities, benefiting from strong economic\par growth because of its use in electronics and photography.\par     Gold        was quoted at $426.25/427.00 after trading as\par low as $424.25.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  The yellow metal was last quoted at\par $426.25/426.95 an ounce in New York.\par     Dealers said gold, which hit a 15-year peak of $430.50 last\par week, was consolidating before charging higher again.\par Resistance was pegged at $432.00 an ounce.\par     "Physical business is very quiet but we see some selling\par back of scrap gold," said Beh Hsia Wah, a dealer at United\par Overseas Bank in Singapore.\par     The Hong Kong dealer said: "There was some physical buying\par from retailers in Hong Kong and Singapore. That's why gold\par moves back to the $425.00 level. But trading was thin because\par of the holiday in Japan."\par     The Tokyo Commodity Exchange's benchmark December 2004 gold\par contract  was quoted at 1,450 yen per gram on Friday, up\par 22 yen. Trading there resumes on Tuesday.\par  \par     Dealers said the market showed no reaction to news that\par Germany had not yet decided on gold sales.\par     Bundesbank President Ernst Welteke said on Sunday said\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 there was no agreement with the government to sell gold, as  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 reported by a newspaper on Sunday, but added it would seek an  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 option under a new gold agreement.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bild am Sonntag said the German government and the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central  \f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  wanted to sell between 400 and 600 tonnes of gold from  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 this year onwards to raise between 4.0 and 7.0 billion euros.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bullion dealers said more central banks were likely to sell  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 gold when the current agreement that limits gold sales to 400  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 tonnes a year expires in September.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A higher quota of 500 to 600 tonnes would likely to send  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 bearish signals to the bullion market, but dealers said rising  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 investor interest in gold could help prevent declines in  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 prices.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market, the dollar rebounded from lows hit  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 last week, aided by caution following the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 aggressive \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to curb the yen's rise.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     The euro        was at $1.2847, off Friday's record high of\par $1.2868 while the dollar was at 106.40 yen .\par     Spot platinum        at $851.00/856.00 and palladium\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 at $202.00/207.00.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040112e01c001mh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
