\par\par \b \uc2 Speculators grow net long yen position - U.S. CFTC.   \b0\par\par\uc2 425 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Januar 2004\par 22:15\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     NEW YORK, Jan 9 (Reuters) - Speculators in IMM Japanese yen\par futures extended a net long position during the week ended Jan.\par 6, data from the Commodity Futures Trading Commission showed.\par     The data from the CFTC's Commitments of Traders report on\par speculative positioning are used by analysts as an indicator of\par future market direction.\par     Extreme net long speculative positions often signal a\par decline in a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , especially if that position conflicts\par with the positioning of more influential commercial players.\par     Speculators generally comprise trend followers seeking to\par pick a precise top or bottom in the market.\par     Yen futures speculators at the Chicago Mercantile Exchange\par extended the net long position to 56,834 contracts for the week\par ended Jan. 6 from 47,664 contracts the prior week.\par     Despite \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's apparently hefty yen-weakening \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par this week, speculators seem to have been eager to push the yen\par up, analysts said.\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "The data suggest that the speculative community seems to\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 be taking a run at the MOF (Japan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ), like   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 a bull at a red flag," said T.J. Marta, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  analyst at   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Citibank in New York.    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     The MOF orders \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which\par is undertaken by the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     JAPANESE YEN (Contracts of 12,500,000 yen)\par              1/06/04 week         12/30/03 week\par    Long          62,753               51,851\par    Short          5,919                4,187\par    Net           56,834               47,664\par     EURO (Contracts of 125,000 euros)\par              1/06/04 week         12/30/03 week\par    Long          36,578               38,530\par    Short          6,668                4,974\par    Net           29,910               33,556\par     POUND STERLING (Contracts of 62,000 pounds sterling)\par              1/06/04 week         12/30/03 week\par    Long          22,009               22,849\par    Short          3,959                2,893\par    Net           18,050               19,956\par     SWISS FRANC (Contracts of 125,000 Swiss francs)\par              1/06/04 week         12/30/03 week\par    Long          21,198               21,637\par    Short          4,993                4,854\par    Net           16,205               16,783\par     CANADIAN DOLLAR (Contracts of 100,000 Canadian dollars)\par              1/06/04 week         12/30/03 week\par    Long          29,498               22,336\par    Short          2,286                3,377\par    Net           27,212               18,959\par     AUSTRALIAN DOLLAR (Contracts of 100,000 Aussie dollars)\par              1/06/04 week         12/30/03 week\par    Long          25,848               26,703\par    Short          1,341                  582\par    Net           24,507               26,121\par     MEXICAN PESO (Contracts of 500,000 pesos)\par              1/06/04 week         12/30/03 week\par    Long          13,046                4,452\par    Short          3,592               14,921\par   