\par\par \b \uc2 Dollar jumps on suspected  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  then slips back.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Naomi Tajitsu  \par \uc2 388 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Januar 2004\par 07:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Jan 9 (Reuters) - The dollar shot up by more than two yen on Friday to its highest level in almost a month after what appeared to be massive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Japanese authorities but it quickly lost half of that gain to trade around 107 yen.   \par \par \uc2  The dollar - recently weighed down by concerns over a bulging U.S. current account deficit - soared to 108.30 yen, its highest level since December 15, from the day's low of 106.18.   \par \par \uc2  "I was looking at my screen and turned away to look at stock prices, and when I turned back, it had shot off the board," said Soichi Okuda, senior economist at Sumitomo Corporation.   \par \par \uc2  Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF) declined comment on whether there had been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2  By 0640 GMT, the dollar had dropped back to 107.01 yen, suggesting to dealers that the effect of any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would continue to be short-lived.   \par \par \uc2  Traders said the BOJ initially stepped in to buy dollars at around 106.20 yen and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  again in heavy amounts after resistance at around 106.50 yen was cleared.   \par \par \uc2  Bankers said they then saw stop-loss buying by foreign operators and traders here, which drove the dollar up to 108.30 yen, before exporters and Japanese life insurance companies stepped in to sell the greenback.   \par \par \uc2  "It started out with \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but with the long weekend coming up, the market repositioned dollar shorts ahead of the U.S. payroll figures. So a lot of it had to do with timing," Okuda said.   \par \par \uc2  The euro was pulled up against the yen, hitting 137.70 yen, a level not seen since July 2003. It subsequently fell back to 136.14 yen.   \par \par \uc2  The single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was slightly weaker against the dollar, trading at $1.2720 versus $1.2756 in late New York.   \par \par \uc2  One market source said Japan, worried that a strong yen could hurt an export-led recovery in its economy, spent about three trillion yen ($28.25 billion) in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday and Tuesday.   \par \par \uc2  However, that did not prevent the dollar from hitting a three-year low of 105.90 yen on Wednesday.   \par \par \uc2  In 2003, the MOF spent a record 20 trillion yen in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . ($1=106.19 yen).   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040109e019001bp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
