\par\par \b \uc2 Dollar jumps two yen on suspected BOJ  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 .   \b0\par\par\uc2 200 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Januar 2004\par 07:08\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Jan 9 (Reuters) - The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  was seen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Friday, pushing the dollar up over two yen on the day to a one-month high, traders said.    \par \par \uc2  The dollar jumped to a high of 108.30 yen  - its highest since December 15 - from the day's low of around 106.18 yen.    \par \par \uc2  By 0538 GMT it was at 107.55/68 yen.    \par \par \uc2  Traders said the BOJ initially stepped in at around 106.20 yen and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  again in heavy amounts after resistance around 106.50 yen was cleared.    \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  declined to comment on the apparent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  but a ministry official said the yen's recent strength was due to speculation and not based on economic fundamentals.    \par \par \uc2  A market source said Japan, worried that a strong yen could hurt an export-led recovery in its economy, spent about three trillion yen ($28.25 billion) in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday and Tuesday.    \par \par \uc2  However, the yen fell to a three-year low of 105.90 yen per dollar on Wednesday.    \par \par \uc2  In 2003, MOF spent a record 20 trillion yen in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . ($1=106.19 Yen).    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040109e019001ad\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
