\par\par \b \uc2 Asian Stocks Rally; Indonesia Ends at All-Time High  \b0\par\par\uc2 596 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Januar 2004\par 13:20\par \uc2 Dow Jones Business News\par \uc2 DJON\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Associated Press   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 HONG KONG -- Stock markets surged across Asia Friday, with Indonesia's key index hitting an all-time high due to falling interest rates and improved economic prospects.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 The Jakarta Stock Exchange Composite Index rose 22.87 points, or 3.1%, to 753.62.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts said the rise was driven by foreign investors lured to Indonesia by falling interest and inflation rates. Last year, investors pushed the Jakarta bourse up 63%, making it Southeast Asia's second-best performer after Thailand.  \par \par \uc2 Tokyo stocks rose to an 11-week high after the dollar jumped against the yen on a suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market by the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The Nikkei Stock Average of 225 issues rose 127.40 points, or 1.18%, to 10,965.05 points -- its highest close since Oct. 21, when it finished at 11,031.52.  \par \par \uc2 The Japanese market got a lift from the greenback's jump, which encouraged buying of Nikkei futures and shares in exporters.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose more than one yen in the afternoon on what market watchers said was likely an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Japanese financial authorities have been aggressively buying the dollar in recent months to keep the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from weakening further against the yen.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar was quoted at 107.04 yen late Friday in Tokyo, up 0.87 yen from 106.17 yen Thursday in Tokyo and also above the 106.17 yen it bought in New York later that day.  \par \par \uc2 In Hong Kong, the blue-chip Hang Seng Index rose 182.21 points, or 1.38%, to 13,385.80 -- its highest close since June 13, 2001. On Thursday, the index had edged up 45.91 points, or 0.4%.  \par \par \uc2 Investors took their cue from Thursday's gains on Wall Street, where the Dow Jones industrial average closed up 63.41, or 0.6%, to 10,592.44, its highest close since March 2002. The tech-laden Nasdaq composite index advanced 22.57 or 1.1%, to 2,100.25, the first time it closed above 2,100 since July 3, 2001.  \par \par \uc2 U.S. stocks rose on signs of an improving business climate in the United States.  \par \par \uc2 Singapore shares closed higher for the 11th straight session at a fresh 33-month high following optimism of an economic rebound and higher corporate profits. The Straits Times Index rose 10.85 points, or 0.6%, to 1,852.53.  \par \par \uc2 South Korean shares closed higher on buying of blue chips by foreign investors. The Korea Composite Stock Price Index, or Kospi, rose 21.12 points, or 2.6%, to 845.27, finishing above 840 for the first time since May 28, 2002.  \par \par \uc2 Philippine shares closed higher on bargain hunting. The 30-company Philippine Stock Exchange Index rose 33.37 points, or 2.2%, to 1,528.87.  \par \par \uc2 Taiwan shares closed at a fresh 20-month high. The Weighted Price Index rose 57.81 points, or 0.94%, to 6,226.98.  \par \par \uc2 New Zealand shares closed higher. The benchmark NZSX-50 Gross Index rose 7.75 points, or 0.3%, to 2,464.746.  \par \par \uc2 Australian shares closed slightly higher. The All Ordinaries Index rose 2.50 points, or 0.08%, to 3,307.10.  \par \par \uc2 Malaysian shares closed higher. The Composite Index of 100 blue chips rose 12.22 points, or 1.5%, to 825.42.  \par \par \uc2 Thai shares closed higher in line with regional markets. The Stock Exchange of Thailand Index rose 9.89 points, or 1.3%, to 783.44.  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJON000020040109e0190000c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
