\par\par \b \uc2 TECHNICALS- \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  market views and key levels.  \b0\par\par\uc2 567 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Januar 2004\par 21:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     NEW YORK, Jan 8 (Reuters) - Following is a selection of\par comments from analysts on important technical developments in\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market.\par     TECHNICAL ANALYST, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  CONCEPTS, NEW YORK:\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2  - EURO/DOLLAR: "Only a close below $1.2475 will put the   \par \par \uc2  seal on a significant bearish reversal. Meanwhile, immediate   \par \par \uc2  support is seen at $1.2575 from a medium-term rising line.   \par \par \uc2  That's followed by the area between $1.2552 and $1.2539. A   \par \par \uc2  pivotal level is then seen at $1.2475. If the ball starts   \par \par \uc2  rolling, then the euro/dollar could easily sink to $1.2366."   \par \par \uc2  - DOLLAR/YEN: "Further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  managed to vault dollar/yen back above the 106.00 yen mark from   \par \par \uc2  a new low of 105.89 yen for the downtrend. Support is now at   \par \par \uc2  this low. However, strong support remains at 105.60 yen from a   \par \par \uc2  50-point pivot that targets 105.10 yen and 106.10 yen.   \par \par \uc2  "Resistance still hovers at 106.40 yen with key resistance   \par \par \uc2  coming from the 50-point pivot at 106.75 yen, which targets   \par \par \uc2  107.25 yen and 106.25 yen. Further resistance resides at 107.50   \par \par \uc2  yen and 107.71 yen. Distant resistance remains at 107.95 yen   \par \par \uc2  from a 50-point pivot that targets 107.45 yen and 108.45 yen."   \par \par \uc2  - DOLLAR/SWISS FRANC: "Dollar/Swiss franc made the   \par \par \uc2  expected recovery on Wednesday and climbed to the highest   \par \par \uc2  levels seen since Dec. 30. The pair will challenge the   \par \par \uc2  resistance of its declining 20-day moving average, now at   \par \par \uc2  around 1.2487 francs, for the first time since Nov. 12. A break   \par \par \uc2  higher would signal a rally to 1.2566 francs and eventually to   \par \par \uc2  1.2633 francs, but this is less likely."   \par \par \uc2  THOMAS FITZPATRICK, CHIEF TECHNICAL ANALYST, CITIFX:   \par \par \uc2  - DOLLAR/YEN: "Trend support is 105.98 yen and resistance   \par \par \uc2  106.75 yen."   \par \par \uc2  - EURO/YEN: "Can correct as far as 132.85 yen initially,   \par \par \uc2  therefore if/when it reaches this level and euro/dollar   \par \par \uc2  continues towards $1.2400, dollar/yen may well begin to   \par \par \uc2  bounce."   \par \par \uc2  - DOLLAR/SWISS FRANC: "If (the dollar were) to close above   \par \par \uc2  1.2548 francs this week it would constitute a bullish weekly   \par \par \uc2  reversal of the low of the move and suggest that this bounce   \par \par \uc2  could extend towards 1.3000 francs."   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid prices at 3:14 p.m. EST (20:14 GMT). All data   \par \par \uc2  takenfrom Reuters calculated from the levels at 4:30 p.m. EST   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                       Last  US Close    %       YTD      2003\par                              07 Jan.  Change %Change    Close\par -------------------------------------------------------------\par Euro/dlr             1.2761   1.2637   +0.98   +1.45   1.2578\par Dlr/yen              106.16   106.24   -0.08   -1.07   107.31\par Euro/yen             135.55   134.29   +0.94   +0.39   135.03\par Dlr/swiss            1.2262   1.2395   -1.07   -1.14   1.2403\par Stg/dlr              1.8313   1.8180   +0.73   +2.59   1.7850\par Dlr/cad              1.2800   1.2891   -0.71   -1.27   1.2965\par Aus/dl