\par\par \b \uc2 Korean won, Canada dollar among top tips for 2004.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Carolyn Cohn  \par \uc2 697 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Januar 2004\par 16:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 LONDON, Jan 8 (Reuters) - Fancy a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  flutter in 2004? Try buying the Korean won or Canadian dollar, or selling the yen in favour of the Swiss franc.  \par \par \uc2 Burnt after a year in which the U.S. dollar underperformed almost every forecast, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategists are preparing new recommendations for this year.  \par \par \uc2 Most expect the dollar to continue to decline in 2004, and are focusing on selling the dollar against Asian or European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  or on the commodity-based \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Australia, New Zealand and Canada, or on trading \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  combinations not involving the dollar at all.  \par \par \uc2 "It's been a tough couple of years for the dollar and it is likely to get much tougher still," said Steve Barrow, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Bear Stearns.  \par \par \uc2 "Our base scenario is for the dollar to fall another 15 percent during this year."  \par \par \uc2 CHINA LEADS THE WAY  \par \par \uc2 A key theme for 2004 is the expected revaluation of China's yuan, amid growth across Southeast Asia.  \par \par \uc2 Japanese authorities' repeated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the past year to prevent the yen from rising increases the appeal of other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the region such as South Korea's won, analysts said.  \par \par \uc2 "The Korean won is a proxy for the whole Asian trade, including China," said Thomas Stolper, global market economist at Goldman Sachs.  \par \par \uc2 "We have a pretty bullish view on Korea domestically, and combined with the Asian revaluation story, the won is a pretty good starting place. It's one of the more liquid \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and it seems to be undervalued."  \par \par \uc2 South Korea's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor said on Thursday that 2004 economic growth would easily meet a target of more than five percent.  \par \par \uc2 The won features twice in Goldman Sachs' top 10 macro trades for 2004.  \par \par \uc2 Goldman recommends buying the won against the dollar , and also buying a one-year call on a basket of Chinese yuan, Indian rupee, Korean won and Taiwanese dollar.  \par \par \uc2 A call option gives the holder the right, but not the obligation, to buy an asset at a future time at a price fixed in advance.  \par \par \uc2 Goldman's other top \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trades are to buy the Swedish crown against the dollar and to buy one commodity \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Australian dollar, against another, the South African rand.  \par \par \uc2 CANADIAN DREAM  \par \par \uc2 Many analysts favour the high yields of the commodity-linked \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which are also benefiting from rising commodity prices.  \par \par \uc2 The Australian dollar was one of the best-performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 2003, but some analysts are picking the Canadian dollar as the one to watch this year.  \par \par \uc2 The Canadian unit has repeatedly hit 10-year highs against the U.S. dollar in recent weeks, strengthening beyond C$1.28 to the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 BNP Paribas sees the Canadian dollar strengthening to C$1.18 per dollar in the fourth quarter, levels last seen in 1992.  \par \par \uc2 Canada's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will increasingly shrug off rate cut expectations, which have previously hampered its progress, analysts said.  \par \par \uc2 Economies such as Canada which enjoy a current account surplus are also poised for gains, analysts added.  \par \par \uc2 "The overall fundamentals are very sound, so a rate cut won't have much impact on the Canadian dollar," said Ian Stannard, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at BNP Paribas.  \par \par \uc2 "The market focus will move away from interest rate differentials to the fiscal situation this year."  \par \par \uc2 EUROPE VS ASIA  \par \par \uc2 Analysts at UBS caution that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the yen will give \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  little leeway to strengthen.  \par \par \uc2 European policymakers have, in contrast, been relatively unconcerned about the runaway strength of European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the dollar, including the euro, pound and Swiss franc.  \par \par \uc2 Both the Swiss franc and the yen are often used as so-called carry trades, borrowed by investors to fund positions in higher-yielding markets.  \par \par \uc2 But expectations of a rise in Switzerland's ultra-low interest rates make the Swiss franc an attractive \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy against the yen, UBS analysts said.  \par \par \uc2 "There are more \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  risks in Asia than in Europe," said Mansoor Mohi-uddin, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at UBS.  \par \par \uc2 "If we get any disappointing data, it will hit global equity markets and Asian countries won't want their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to strengthen."   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040108e018002s6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
