\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar recovers ground versus euro ahead of ECB.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Burton Frierson  \par \uc2 606 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Januar 2004\par 11:53\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 LONDON, Jan 8 (Reuters) - The dollar won some respite against the euro on Thursday as nervousness the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might signal concern over the euro's record-breaking rally prompted investors to reduce bets on the greenback's slide.  \par \par \uc2 The ECB is expected to leave interest rates unchanged at Thursday's policy meeting and the market focus is on whether bank chief Jean-Claude Trichet will use a news conference at 1330 GMT to signal a shift in his hitherto relaxed attitude to the euro's rise.  \par \par \uc2 The euro has leapt more than 10 percent against the dollar in the past two months, bringing its gains over the past two years to more than 40 percent. Business groups have warned that euro strength is hurting European exporters and denting growth prospects.  \par \par \uc2 "If there is going to be a comment from the ECB it is more likely to focus on the speed of adjustment, as opposed to the level itself," said Shahab Jalinoos, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at ABN Amro.  \par \par \uc2 "But the market was worried anyway that euro/dollar was over-extended because most momentum based indicators were telling you that the trend was over-stretched."  \par \par \uc2 The euro eased to $1.2562 in early European trade, down about half a percent on the day and 2-1/2 cents from record peaks scaled on Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar was steady near three-year lows around 106.00 yen, with dealers wary of continued dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Earlier on Thursday, European Union 