\par\par \b \uc2 Tokyo's Nikkei at 2-month high on techs, banks.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Eriko Amaha  \par \uc2 602 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Januar 2004\par 08:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Jan 8 (Reuters) - Tokyo's Nikkei stock average snapped a two-day losing streak to end at a two-month high on Thursday as a rally in the U.S. Nasdaq index boosted investor confidence and sent Sharp Corp and other technology shares higher.  \par \par \uc2 Bank shares were also sought after the news on Wednesday that Sumitomo Trust & Banking Co would become the second top bank in Japan to fully pay back state funds.  \par \par \uc2 "The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  is loaded with money to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market," said Mitsushige Akino, chief fund manager at Ichiyoshi Investment Management Co Ltd. "The market view is that if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  can smooth falls in the dollar against the yen, Japanese corporate earnings should not be affected that much."  \par \par \uc2 The Nikkei average closed up 0.74 percent at 10,837.65, its highest close since November 4.  \par \par \uc2 Masaharu Sakudo, an adviser at Tachibana Securities, said the Nikkei may be ready for another rally after having priced in the effect of the recent strengthening of the yen.  \par \par \uc2 "The market has factored in a dollar/yen level of 105," he said.  \par \par \uc2 The broader TOPIX index also rose 0.51 percent to 1,056.92.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said technology shares have been in a long correction phase over the past couple of months under the threat of a strong yen, but they are now looked upon more favourably as demand for digital electronics products is growing at home and abroad.  \par \par \uc2 Sharp, the world's largest maker of liquid crystal display (LCD) televisions, was up 2.72 percent at 1,778 yen, just three percent off of last year's high of 1,833 yen.  \par \par \uc2 The stock also was lifted by Sharp's announcement on Thursday that it would have a second production line for large-screen LCD TVs at its plant from August 2004 and would invest 130 billion yen ($1.22 billion) in its LCD business for the 2004/05 fiscal year.  \par \par \uc2 Another leading digital products maker, Matsushita Electric Industrial Co, gained 2.14 percent to 1,526 yen.  \par \par \uc2 Among Sharp's other peers, NEC Corp rose 2.25 percent to 819 yen while Toshiba Corp climbed 2.87 percent to 430 yen.  \par \par \uc2 Parts makers also drew buyers, with Sanyo Electric Co Ltd, which has a strong battery business, up 1.95 percent at 575 yen.  \par \par \uc2 Kyocera Corp, an electronic components maker, advanced 3.38 percent to 7,650 yen, after the company's president told Reuters in an interview on Wednesday that its earnings for the year to March would likely exceed projections.  \par \par \uc2 "Parts for digital products are in great demand and makers cannot catch up," said Kenichi Azuma, an equity strategist at Cosmo Securities Co Ltd.  \par \par \uc2 Importers benefited from the strong yen as Oji Paper Co climbed 2.5 percent to 739 yen and Nippon Unipac Holding rose 2.99 percent to 586,000 yen. Sumitomo Trust's public fund repayment plan was good news for the banking sector.  \par \par \uc2 Sumitomo Trust rose 0.98 percent to 616 yen. UFJ Holdings rang up 1.58 percent to 515,000 yen and Mitsubishi Tokyo Financial Group rose 2.46 percent to 833,000 yen.  \par \par \uc2 Advancers outpaced decliners, 954 to 451 in active trade.  \par \par \uc2 Trade volume grew to 1.426 billion shares changing hands on the first section of the Tokyo Stock Exchange, compared with 1.2 billion shares on Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 Trade value also stood at 1.26 trillion yen, the highest since December 12.  \par \par \uc2 ($1=106.21 Yen).  \par \par \uc2 . (C) Reuters Limited 2004.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040108e0180015y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
