\par\par \b \uc2 Dollar rises as traders await ECB's Trichet.   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Hideyuki Sano   \par \uc2 672 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Januar 2004\par 07:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Jan 8 (Reuters) - The dollar won a reprieve on Thursday, rising against the euro on speculation the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (ECB) chief might warn against the recent rapid rise of the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 The greenback was stuck near three-year lows versus the yen amid wariness about Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with few traders eager to challenge \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's apparent determination to block the dollar's decline.   \par \par \uc2 Still, traders said a strong rebound in the dollar was unlikely as the market is deeply concerned about the yawning U.S. current account deficit and as benchmark U.S. interest rates are likely to stay at a 45-year-low in the near-term.   \par \par \uc2 As of 0305 GMT, the euro had slipped to around $1.2590 from 1.2631/37 in late U.S. trade. It was down more than two cents from a record high of 1.2813 on Tuesday.   \par \par \uc2 The euro also fell against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to 133.65 yen from 134.10.   \par \par \uc2 "There is a worry that (ECB President Jean-Claude) Trichet may say something like 'a rapid rise in the euro' or 'a rapid fall of the dollar is not desirable'," said Etsuko Yamashita, chief economist at Sumitomo Mitsui Banking Corp.   \par \par \uc2 Trichet will hold a news conference at 1330 GMT after the ECB's monetary policy meeting. Most economists think the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will keep policy unchanged.   \par \par \uc2 But Yamashita also said that Trichet might not sound any warning, in which case the euro could resume its rally.   \par \par \uc2 Amid wariness over Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the dollar was locked around 106.20 yen , hardly changed from late U.S. trade and off the three-year low hit on Wednesday.   \par \par \uc2 The greenback suddenly fell below the closely watched 106 yen level on Wednesday to hit the low of 105.90 yen , before resurfacing almost instantly.   \par \par \uc2 There was confusion over why the blip occurred, with some dealers saying it was due to a glitch on the EBS trading system, but banks in Tokyo - both foreign and domestic - used 105.90 as the overnight low.   \par \par \uc2 NO CHOICE ON \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 Traders suspect the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) was \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  around 106 yen during U.S. trade to prop up the dollar.   \par \par \uc2 Japanese authorities, seen desperate to keep the dollar away from the technically and psychologically important 105 yen level, spent around three trillion yen ($28.25 billion) in the first two days of this week on yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a market source told Reuters on Wednesday.   \par \par \uc2 "That's an amazing amount," said a dealer at a British Bank.   \par \par \uc2 Japan spent a total 20 trillion yen throughout 2003 in trying to keep the yen in check.   \par \par \uc2 Traders expect Japan to keep stepping into the market.   \par \par \uc2 "They have no choice but to continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But I don't think they are trying to protect a certain level, such as 106 yen, as some in the media are speculating," said Yoshiharu Yanagisawa, vice president at State Street Bank.   \par \par \uc2 "They are just conducting a smoothing \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It's difficult to contain the yen's rise when global capital is moving away from the U.S. to the rest of the world," he said.   \par \par \uc2 Many traders expect the dollar to fall despite \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , given nagging worries about the health of the U.S. balance of payments.   \par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, the International Monetary Fund (IMF) said growing U.S. deficits raised the risk of an abrupt drop in the value of the dollar, which could hit U.S. and global economic growth. The IMF said it was a risk that "cannot be ignored".   \par \par \uc2 "I think the market will test a break under 100 yen by the end of March," said Yoshiyasu Naruse, head of corporate \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales at HSBC Ltd.   \par \par \uc2 A median forecast of 49 analysts polled by Reuters saw the dollar holding steady at 106 yen in the coming month but slipping to 105 in three months, 104 in six and 102 by the end of the year.    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040108e0180011x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
