\par\par \b \uc2 Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Euro Falls Vs Dollar, Yen On Profit-Taking  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Leika Kihara  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 811 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Januar 2004\par 06:31\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The euro fell against the dollar and the yen in Asia Thursday, as traders adjusted their positions to reap short-term gains amid growing wariness about the single European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent fast-paced ascent.  \par \par \uc2 After rising to $1.2656, the euro turned down and fell to around $1.2586 on persistent profit-taking by commercial banks and short-term speculators. The euro also lost ground against the yen to fall as low as Y133.56.  \par \par \uc2 "Traders are becoming restless about bidding up the euro further," said Resona Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager Shigehiro Kamimura. "They're starting to realize that the market has tilted too much toward dollar weakness with no good reason."  \par \par \uc2 The dollar held steady against the yen after its brief dip to a 40-month low of Y105.91 in overnight New York trade, moving in a tight range in the low Y106s throughout the Tokyo session.  \par \par \uc2 Suspected bids by Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  firmly supported the dollar's downside around Y106.15, but the topside was capped around Y106.40 on speculator-led offers, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 Many market players expect the MOF to continue \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent further yen gains from hurting \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's export-led economic recovery.  \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, some traders wondered whether the euro may be entering a minor adjustment phase after its sharp rise to a record high of $1.2813 on Jan. 6., which was due in part to the market's strong distaste for the greenback amid lingering geopolitical concerns in Iraq and the massive U.S. trade and budget deficits.  \par \par \uc2 "The tide may shift in favor of the dollar for a while," as supply and demand now seem to warrant a correction of the euro to around $1.2500, Uemura said.  \par \par \uc2 But he added that the long-term trend remains bullish for the euro, predicting that it will resume its upward march toward new record highs after the wave of profit-taking runs its course.  \par \par \uc2 Tokyo market players are keeping close tabs on what European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Jean-Claude Trichet has to say about the euro's strength in a press conference after the ECB's board meeting later in the day.  \par \par \uc2 Any warning against the potential negative impact of the euro's strength on European economies could put further downward pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 At 0515 GMT, the dollar was quoted at Y106.17, below Y106.27 late Wednesday in New York and Tokyo.  \par \par \uc2 The euro was at $1.2592, lower than $1.2640 late Wednesday in New York. The euro was at $1.2719 in Tokyo Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 Against the yen, the euro was quoted at Y133.67, down from Y134.25 in New York late Wednesday. The euro was at Y135.12 in Tokyo late Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 Sterling was at $1.8138, down from $1.8180 in New York and lower than $1.8199 in Tokyo Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 While most market players still believe the dollar will eventually slip below Y106 again, some think downside risk may have become somewhat limited on the presumed persistence of MOF \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and growing prospects of an upward correction in the greenback.  \par \par \uc2 Last year, the Japanese authorities sold a record Y20.05 trillion to cap the yen in order to help Japanese exporters.  \par \par \uc2 The ministry is gearing up for a bigger battle by bolstering reserve funds for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and has received approval to boost its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  arsenal by Y21 trillion this fiscal year and by Y40 trillion next fiscal year.  \par \par \uc2 Some analysts estimate that the MOF has already spent around Y3 trillion in \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the first week of January.  \par \par \uc2 The next crucial event for gauging the MOF's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  stance could come at the meeting of officials from the Group of Seven leading industrial economies in Florida next month.  \par \par \uc2 Views are emerging in the market that the ministry may be forced to slow the pace of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  before and during the meeting to avoid being criticized by Japan's G7 counterparts as trying to intentionally cheapen the yen.  \par \par \uc2 But Yasunari Ueno, chief market economist at Mizuho Securities, doesn't expect this to happen. "The ministry will likely \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  persistently if the dollar enters the Y100-Y105 zone, since a fall below Y100 would mean a significant negative impact on the Japanese economy," he said.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    -By Leika Kihara, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; leika.kihara@dowjones.com   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Alastair Gale  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The chart of late Tokyo \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rates that accompanied Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been replaced with an enhanced \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fixture that is updated hourly.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Subscribers can find this table:  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -On Telerate pages 4046 and 1087.  \f28 \par \par \uc2