\par\par \b \uc2 POLL-Yen seen rising despite resistance from Japan.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Christina Fincher  \par \uc2 494 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Januar 2004\par 13:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 LONDON, Jan 7 (Reuters) - The yen is set to remain on a upward track against the dollar in the coming year as Japan fights a losing battle to keep its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  competitive against a tumbling greenback, according to \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategists.  \par \par \uc2 The median forecast of 49 analysts polled by Reuters saw the yen holding steady at 106 to the dollar in the coming month but rising to 105 in three months, 104 in six and 102 by the end of the year.  \par \par \uc2 Some even saw the yen rising to the psychological 100 marker against the dollar, a level last touched in 1995.  \par \par \uc2 Asia is expected to be a big beneficiary of the global upturn and analysts say Japan will struggle to offset rising foreign demand for its assets by selling yen on the foreign exchanges.  \par \par \uc2 "Japan cannot prop up the dollar single-handedly but the aim of its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is to deflect upward pressure on the yen for as long as it can," said Stephen Jen, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Morgan Stanley.  \par \par \uc2 Japan threw a record 20 trillion yen at the foreign exchanges last year, fearing a rise in the yen could derail the country's export-led recovery.  \par \par \uc2 Japanese authorities have also been spotted conducting heavy yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  this week as the dollar extended its broad-based decline. One market source told Reuters Japan had spent around three trillion yen on Monday and Tuesday alone.  \par \par \uc2 POLITICAL ISSUES  \par \par \uc2 In a move to secure more \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  funds, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced last month that it would raise the borrowing limit on its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  account to 140 trillion yen in the fiscal year starting next April from 79 trillion yen.  \par \par \uc2 However, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policy of yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has drawn criticism in international quarters since it has forced free-floating \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , notably the euro, to bear a disproportional weight of the dollar's adjustment.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts say it may become harder for \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to justify \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as its recovery gathers pace or if China takes steps to allow its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to appreciate.  \par \par \uc2 At the moment, China - Japan's second-largest trading partner - pegs its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 "Since China is not likely to give up its dollar peg, an appreciation of the yen against the dollar also means an appreciation against the yuan," said Dieter Wermuth at UFJ Bank in London.  \par \par \uc2 "Yen fundamentals argue for further appreciation against the dollar, so \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  will continue."  \par \par \uc2 If China continues to drag its feet on the issue of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  revaluation, European finance ministers are likely to put growing pressure on Japan to accept a greater weight of the dollar's decline when Group of Seven finance ministers meet in Boca Raton, Florida early next month.  \par \par \uc2 "The G7 could be ugly if Europe tries to fight on the issue of burden-sharing, but Japan is not afraid of pressure from Europe," said Morgan Stanley's Jen.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040107e017002s6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
