\par\par \b \uc2 BOJ spent Y3 trln in  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  this week-source.  \b0\par\par\uc2 304 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Januar 2004\par 10:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Jan 7 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , worried that a strong yen could hurt an export-led recovery in its economy, spent about three trillion yen ($28.3 billion) in the first two days of this week to hold the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  down, a market source said on Wednesday. That figure compares with some 20 trillion yen ($188 billion) spent on yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the whole of 2003. The source said the Bank of Japan, acting on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF), sold about 2.6 trillion yen on Monday. Despite the massive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the dollar hit a three-year low of 106.06 yen later that day.  \par \par \uc2 About 400 billion yen was spent on Tuesday when the dollar touched a low of 106.09 yen, the source said.  \par \par \uc2 In late Tokyo trade on Wednesday, the dollar was holding just above that level, at around 106.20 yen.  \par \par \uc2 The Japanese authorities are thought by some analysts to be desperate to prevent the dollar from falling below 105 yen, since that would trigger heavy options-related selling of the U.S. unit, but traders say it is only a matter of time before it breaks through 106 yen.  \par \par \uc2 In a move to secure more \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  funds, the MOF announced last month that it would raise the borrowing limit on its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  account to 140 trillion yen in the fiscal year starting next April from 79 trillion yen.  \par \par \uc2 As a stopgap measure to avoid a funding crunch before parliament approves the raising of the borrowing limit, the ministry has arranged a repo deal with the Bank of Japan in which it can get funds by selling foreign bonds to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , buying the paper back at a later date. ($1=106.18 Yen).   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040107e0170028r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
