\par\par \b \uc2 Japan aims to stop dlr fall below 106 yen - Nikkei.   \b0\par\par\uc2 295 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Januar 2004\par 21:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, Jan 6 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Tuesday to curb yen strength and try to avoid a plunge of the dollar below the 106 yen mark, Nikkei's Nihon Keizai Shimbun Wednesday morning edition reported.   \par \par \uc2 "\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monetary authorities \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Tuesday for a second straight day in a bid to curb a further rise in the yen," Nikkei said.   \par \par \uc2 "With the dollar falling to 106.09 yen at one point, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the Bank of Japan determined that the breach of the 106 yen mark would send the dollar into free fall, and quickly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell yen," Nikkei said.   \par \par \uc2 Technical analysts said there are some key support levels for the dollar not far below the 106 yen area.   \par \par \uc2 "I have, and have had for almost six months, a 105.70 yen to 105.50 yen target (for the dollar). That is a big technical target," said Jordan Kotick, technical strategist with JP Morgan in New York.   \par \par \uc2 But that is not the last line of defense, which once broken would allow the dollar to embark on a sharp decline against the yen, he told Reuters.   \par \par \uc2 "The level on dollar/yen where the dollar would come in to free fall is a huge level and it comes in just above 101 yen," a low from November 1999," Kotick said.   \par \par \uc2 "If you take that out, from a technical perspective you really open up the downside," Kotick added.   \par \par \uc2 "Despite such efforts (by Japan to curb yen strength), the yen is likely to face continued upward pressure due to the dollar's weakness amid lingering concerns about terrorism and the U.S. current account deficit," Nikkei said.    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040106e016004cr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
