\par\par \b \uc2 ODJ Debt Futures Supported By Reports Of Dollar  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 308 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Januar 2004\par 14:59\par \uc2 Dow Jones Commodities Service\par \uc2 DJCS\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par By Allen Sykora \par     Chicago, Jan. 6 (OsterDowJones) - Ideas that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central-bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par flows into dollars will work their way into mid-length maturities of \par government securities has enabled debt futures to open higher, analysts said. \par     At 0753 CT (1353 GMT), Mar 10-year notes were up 11.5 ticks at 111-21.5, \par Mar Treasury bonds were up 16 ticks at 108-12, and Jun Eurodollars were up 3 \par basis points at 98.555. \par     As the U.S. dollar has continued its slide, the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reportedly \par has been \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on behalf of the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , in order to keep the yen \par from becoming too muscular and hurting Japan's export-oriented economy. There \par have been estimates that the BOJ spent more than $5 billion Monday and another \par $5 billion to $7 billion Tuesday. \par     There is market speculation that perhaps some other Asian central banks \par might be trying to help the BOJ, said David Hightower, president of the \par Hightower Report newsletter. Whatever the case, when central banks \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par buy dollars, they tend to put them to work in the government securities market. \par     "They're into the middle maturities and not necessarily the bonds," said \par Hightower. "But it has been a massive \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  flow by the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . \par They're not going to give up." \par     A series of economic reports is on the calendar for 0900 CT (1500 GMT) \par Tuesday - the Institute for Supply Management's non-manufacturing index, \par factory orders and the monthly Challenger layoff report. The consensus \par forecast calls for the headline index in the ISM report to increase to 61 in \par December from 60.1 in November, while November factory orders are expected to \par fall 1.5%. \par  \par    --- \par Allen Sykora, OsterDowJones \par sykora@bendcable.com \par  \par Copyright 2004 OsterDowJones Commodity News (ODJ). All rights reserved. \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 61060  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCS000020040106e01600071\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
