\par\par \b \uc2 Dollar hits new low vs euro, BOJ seen stepping in.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Hideyuki Sano  \par \uc2 511 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Januar 2004\par 04:21\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Jan 5 (Reuters) - The dollar hit a record low versus the euro on Monday on nagging worries about the gaping U.S. trade balance that characterised its weakness last year.   \par \par \uc2  The greenback was more resilient versus the yen after an erratic jump that many dealers suspect was caused by the Japanese authorities stepping in to buy the dollar. The dollar, whose value fell 17 percent against the euro and nine percent versus the yen last year, has shown no sign of a rebound, with few in the market expecting any dents to the U.S. current account and fiscal deficits this year.   \par \par \uc2  "The market is energetic as market players are ready to take new positions at the start of the new year," said Seiya Nakajima, chief economist at Itochu Corp.   \par \par \uc2  The euro hit a new high of $1.2672 and was standing around $1.2655 by 0300 GMT, up about 0.5 percent from Friday's late U.S. levels around 1.2585/89.   \par \par \uc2  The common \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit a five-month high against the yen around 135.60 yen   \par \par \uc2  The dollar also briefly fell to a four-week low of 106.76 yen at which point the Japanese authorities were seen stepping in.   \par \par \uc2  The greenback briefly shot up to 107.38 yen but gains were pared quickly. At 0300 GMT, it was at around 107.00 yen, slightly below late U.S. levels of 107.05.   \par \par \uc2  STOCKS SEND SHIVER   \par \par \uc2  Some traders jumped on comments by Federal Reserve Governor Ben Bernanke to sell the dollar.   \par \par \uc2  Bernanke said on Sunday that while the U.S. economy appeared to have turned a corner, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was right to hold interest rates at 45-year lows given the low rate of underlying inflation.   \par \par \uc2  Traders said the dollar was also bruised by a rise in Tokyo share prices. The Nikkei average ended a shortened half-day session up 1.39 percent.   \par \par \uc2  "The dollar continues to be weighed down by a rise in the Nikkei and that should be another reason for the market to cap any gains," said Junya Tanase, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at JP Morgan Chase.   \par \par \uc2  Although many dealers are wary of Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , they also say that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is unlikely to turn the dollar around.   \par \par \uc2  "When the dollar is falling broadly, it is unlikely to rise for long against the yen even if there's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Takashi Toyahara, \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager at Nomura Securities.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold a record 20 trillion yen ($187 billion) in 2003 to stem an export-damaging rise in its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2  Japan's top financial diplomat, Zembei Mizoguchi, said on Monday that the Japanese authorities remained ready to step into the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market if there was a danger of volatility.   \par \par \uc2  "We will take appropriate measures when necessary. There is no change in our position" Mizoguchi, vice finance minister for international affairs, told reporters as he arrived for work.   \par \par \uc2  In other trade, sterling rose to an 11-year high of $1.7963. ($1=106.99 yen).   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040105e015000xe\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
