\par\par \b \uc2 GLOBAL MARKETS-Dlr hits new low versus euro, driving up gold.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Ramthan Hussain  \par \uc2 672 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Januar 2004\par 04:01\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Jan 5 (Reuters) - The dollar sank to a record low against the euro on Monday, driven by persistent fears over the widening U.S. current account deficit, sending gold prices to their highest in nearly 14 years.   \par \par \uc2  But suspected yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  helped the dollar jump against the yen with the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  touching a session high of around 107.35 yen after falling to around 106.75, near its three-year low.   \par \par \uc2  The euro hit a record peak of $1.2672 before retreating to trade around 1.2654 at 0255 GMT. Dealers said a defence of low U.S. interest rates from a top Federal Reserve official added pressure on the dollar.   \par \par \uc2  Tokyo stocks opened trade for the new year up more than one percent, catching up on the gains made in global stocks while Japan was on holiday. The gains were led by exporters such as Matsushita Electric Industrial Co, and banks.   \par \par \uc2  Shares in troubled LG Card fell their daily 15 percent limit after South Korea's biggest card issuer said it could run out of money again if lenders failed to agree an immediate $4.2 billion rescue plan, despite reassuring comments from the finance minister.   \par \par \uc2  Other Asian share markets were mixed with the MSCI index of Asia-Pacific shares outside Japan up 0.4 percent. The index jumped 44 percent last year.   \par \par \uc2  A Federal Reserve Governor, Ben Bernanke, told a meeting of the American Economic Association in San Diego on Sunday that while the U.S. economy appeared to have turned a corner, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was right to hold interest rates at 45-year lows given the low rate of underlying inflation.   \par \par \uc2  Bernanke told the conference he did not see much chance of a "dollar crisis" developing in which the value of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept plunging.   \par \par \uc2  Sterling rose to an 11-year high of around $1.7961.   \par \par \uc2  DIGITAL-LED RECOVERY   \par \par \uc2  The dollar was earlier hit by a rise in Tokyo share prices. The Nikkei average rose 1.4 precent at 10,825.17 in a shortened half-day session.   \par \par \uc2  Electronics giant Sony Corp rose 1.9 percent while Matsushita, the maker of Panasonic brand goods, and Canon Inc, gained around one percent.   \par \par \uc2  "The current recovery is often dubbed as one led by digital goods. This will be maintained this year as well, with their sales and earnings seen expanding," said Masaki Iso, chief investment officer at Yasuda Asset Management.   \par \par \uc2  South Korean stocks dipped 0.1 percent on worries over the problems at LG Card, which also sent shares of Shinhan Financial Group, the parent of Shinhan Bank - an LG creditor - down over two percent.   \par \par \uc2  Australian shares shed 0.4 percent pressured by Santos Ltd. The oil and gas producer fell more than four percent after it said a fire at its South Australian gas plant would cut its net profit by A$25 million.   \par \par \uc2  GLITTERING GOLD   \par \par \uc2  Spot gold hit $418.00 an ounce for the first time since February 1990 as the strong euro made the precious metal a better bargain for Europeans.   \par \par \uc2  At 0255 GMT, gold was quoted at $416.75/417.50 an ounce, compared with London's Friday afternoon fix of $415.25.   \par \par \uc2  "It can get to $420 today, I guess," Commonwealth Bank of Australia commodities specialist David Thurtell said.   \par \par \uc2  Japanese government bond prices fell in line with the firmer stocks with the yield on the benchmark 256th 10-year JGBs rising four basis points to 1.4 percent.   \par \par \uc2  Traders said big losses in U.S. Treasury prices on Friday also made market participants uneasy about bidding up JGB prices.   \par \par \uc2  U.S. Treasury prices fell sharply on Friday after a report showing surprising manufacturing strength encouraged markets to expect an eventual interest rate rise by the Federal Reserve.   \par \par \uc2  But this was tempered by Bernanke's comments about stable prices that would signal less pressure on Fed policymakers to raise interest rates.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040105e015000ul\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
