\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  Spent Record Y20.057T in 2003  \highlight22\uc2 Forex Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 303 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Dezember 2003\par 11:29\par \uc2 Dow Jones Business News\par \uc2 DJON\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's government spent a record Y20.057 trillion \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market this year to keep the yen from rising too sharply, \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  data released Tuesday show.  \par \par \uc2 In December alone, the ministry said it ordered the Bank of Japan to sell Y2.252 trillion worth of the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The total \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  amount for 2003 is far bigger than the last record amount of Y7.64 trillion in 1999, and highlights Tokyo's aggressive campaign to prevent a yen surge.  \par \par \uc2 Finance Ministry officials fear a sharply higher yen could undermine exports, one of the main drivers of Japan's current economic recovery.  \par \par \uc2 The heavy yen-selling has caused the government to get close to its legal limit for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but the ministry has taken steps to procure additional funding.  \par \par \uc2 It is set to raise its Y79 trillion funding limit for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Y21 trillion to Y100 trillion this fiscal year ending March, and then to Y140 trillion next fiscal year. The ministry is waiting for Parliament to approve the increases sometime early next year.  \par \par \uc2 To take care of any emergency funding needs which may arise in the meantime, the government has also asked the Bank of Japan to lend up to Y10 trillion in funds by buying U.S. Treasury bonds from the ministry under repurchase agreements.  \par \par \uc2 Despite the heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year, however, the yen on Tuesday was trading at Y106.99 to the dollar around 1000 GMT, compared with around Y119.90 at the end of last year. Some traders predict the dollar will head even lower due to worries about the twin U.S. trade and budget deficits.  \par \par \uc2 -By Miyako Takebe, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; miyako.takebe@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJON000020031230dzcu00006\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
