\par\par \b \uc2 Dow Jones Asia-Pacific Top Stories Sked For Dec 30  \b0\par\par\uc2 918 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Dezember 2003\par 10:05\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 Following are the top Asia-Pacific stories featured on Dow Jones Newswires as of 0900 GMT, along with items expected later in the day. Please direct any questions or comments to asianewseds@dowjones.com or by phone on 65-6415-4020.  \par \par \uc2 MACRO/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /FIXED INCOME  \par \par \uc2 SEOUL: South Korea's economic blueprint for 2004 underscores the difficulties the government faces in the new year amid mounting household debt and a deepening crisis in the credit-card sector. Various data released Tuesday further highlighted that economic woes, including credit card problems which had dragged the world's 12th largest economy into a recession this year, will continue to overshadow the economy next year as well. (WRAP will run by around 0930 GMT)  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO: \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  data will likely show that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent a record sum \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market this year in an effort to keep the yen from rising too sharply. (Story will run after data is released at 1000 GMT)  \par \par \uc2 KARACHI: Pakistan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Tuesday the economy is on track to achieve most macroeconomic goals set for the current fiscal year, with the gross domestic product likely to exceed targeted growth of 5.3%. In its review of the first quarter of fiscal 2003-2004, which began in July, State Bank of Pakistan said industrial growth had been robust in the period, leading other sectors of the economy. ("Pakistan Ctrl Bk," first take ran at 0705 GMT)  \par \par \uc2 HANOI: Vietnam's trade deficit widened to $541 million in December from $288 million in the same month a year earlier, the General Statistics Office said Tuesday. ("Vietnam/Trade," first take ran at 0900 GMT)  \par \par \uc2 TAIPEI: Taiwan High Speed Rail Corp., the biggest build-operate-transfer project on the island, said Tuesday its shareholders had approved a plan to raise NT$21.8 billion through a private placement of preferred stock. ("Taiwan High Speed Rail," first take ran at 0408 GMT)  \par \par \uc2 BANGKOK: Thailand's exports remained robust in November due mainly to buoyant exports to China and Asean countries, but manufacturing production decelerated slightly, the Bank of Thailand said Tuesday. (DATA SNAP will run by around 0915 GMT)  \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG: Local banks are buying short-dated Exchange Fund bills despite a negative yield on the quasi-government paper. Traders say the phenomenon is the result of an interbank market flush with surplus funds combined with the need for banks to buy EF paper to meet daily settlement requirements. (Story will run by around 1015 GMT)  \par \par \uc2 =\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  MARKET ROUNDUP: The dollar was shaky against the yen and the euro in Asia Tuesday, Tokyo's last trading day of the year, though it held above overnight lows partly due to fears of Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Dollar bearishness, stemming broadly from concern over the U.S. twin fiscal and current account deficits, continued to dominate the market, keeping the euro afloat near $1.2500 and the yen hovering near Y107 for most of the session. ("Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 :Dlr Shaky Vs Majors;\b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  Fears Support," ran at 0542 GMT)  \par \par \uc2 EQUITIES  \par \par \uc2 SEOUL: As widely expected, the auction to sell South Korea's cash-strapped LG Card Co. failed Tuesday. Creditors now need to reach an agreement on a proposed joint management plan whereby they will convert 4 trillion won of debt into equity. An agreement could come as early as Tuesday night. ("Auction To Sell LG Card Fails; To Decide On Joint Mgmt," first take ran at 0818 GMT; WRAP will run if agreement is reached)  \par \par \uc2 =ASIAN STOCK FOCUS: Gamuda Bhd. remains the top buy in the Malaysian construction sector despite a setback following the postponement of a 14.5 billion ringgit railway project, analysts say. ("=ASIAN STOCK FOCUS: Buy Malaysia Gamuda Despite Rail Woes," ran at 0211 GMT)  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO: Yoshinoya D&C Co., a major Japanese operator of "gyudon" beef-bowl restaurants, announced Tuesday a series of steps to cope with a possible shortage of imported meat resulting from a ban on U.S. beef. It will stop operating some 174 restaurants late at night, and suspend \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  of some 123 restaurants during the year-end and new-year holidays and also cancel planned sales-promotion efforts. ("Yoshinoya Announces Steps To Cope With US-Beef Import Ban," ran at 0339 GMT)  \par \par \uc2 JAKARTA: PT Telekomunikasi Indonesia said Tuesday that it may have to reduce its previously stated 2002 net income by up to 5% due to a reaudit that is currently in progress. Telkom, the nation's largest phone company, said in a statement it expects to complete the reaudit of 2002 accounts by the end of January. ("Indonesia's Telkom 2002 Net May Fall 5% On Reaudit," ran at 0826 GMT)  \par \par \uc2 SHANGHAI: BNP Paribas S.A. said Tuesday regulators have approved its plan to launch a joint venture fund management company in China with major securities firm Shenyin & Wanguo Securities Corp. ("China Regulator Approves BNP Paribas Asset Management JV," ran at 0830 GMT)  \par \par \uc2 SHANGHAI: Lanzhou Aluminum Co., a leading aluminum producer in China, said Tuesday it plans to raise up to 1 billion yuan through a rights issue to finance its technology upgrade. ("China Lanzhou Aluminum Sets CNY1B, 150M Shr Rights Issue," ran at 0133 GMT)  \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG: MegaInfo, a subsidiary of Growth Enterprise Market-listed Vodatel Networks announces details of proposed listing on GEM at 0830 GMT press conference. The company, headquartered in Macau, develops digital image processing management applications. (Story will run by around 0915 GMT)  \par \par \uc2 62550  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020031230dzcu0007j\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exchange or fx or forex or currenc*) and (interven* or operation*) and (japan near10 interven*) and (rst=trtw or rst=tprw or rst=tdjw) and (central bank or ministry of finance or treasury ministry or monetary authority)\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Datum\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 01/01/1995 bis 21/08/2023\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\br